   Anyone who makes a private work must notify R3d of its existence, what it
   is and why it is private, giving a meaningful reason, by opening an issue
   at https://github.com/R3disme/jotiglobe/issues (or in another way agreed
   with R3d). Keeping the code private only to avoid sharing it is not a
   meaningful reason: R3d may then refuse the private use and ask for the
   source code to be made public. JotiGlobe was made for all scouts, and we
   wish that all scouts can continue to enjoy the works made from it.

4. Permitted private works. The organisations below may keep private works
   without giving a reason. They must still notify R3d of their existence and
